[agent] |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
[agent] | corr with label | 0.090 | 0.077 | 0.148 | 0.146 | **0.9932** | 0.142 |
[agent] - f5's correlation with the label (0.9932) dwarfs every other feature (0.08–0.15).
[agent] - The two classes are **completely non-overlapping** on f5: label=0 lies in [-0.428, 0.398] (mean ≈ 0.01), label=1 lies in [2.064, 2.833] (mean ≈ 2.50). There is a clean ~1.6-wide gap between them.
[agent] - A single threshold `f5 > 1.0` classifies **all 800/800 rows correctly (100%)**.
[agent] No real feature separates a binary outcome perfectly with one threshold — f5 was clearly computed from post-outcome data, so it leaks the label. All other features show heavy class overlap (e.g., f3 means -0.056 vs 0.234) consistent with legitimate, weakly-predictive features.
